* RESET.COM - RESET THE EMULATED MACHINE

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* RESET.COM - RESET THE EMULATED MACHINE

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:RESET

Requests a hardware reset through cpmsim control port 160. It restarts the
emulated machine; it is not a directory refresh or resident disk reset.

Do not use while a caller is connected or while files are being written.
For a controlled host stop use SYSUTLS:BYEBYE after activity finishes.
Resident R performs a different, disk-reset operation. MOUNT handles
collection volume changes.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
